{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792419318,"nonce":"0T+oGAioAb8rykC5r/10fe8XRCg=","title":"A model's textures should come from block-compressed files, not be decoded and encoded as the program runs","message":"**Problem**\nA mesh texture was made at run time: the image decoded (a 4096 by 4096 JPEG or PNG is 64 MB of RGBA), shrunk in a page, resampled to every mip level and, on a desktop, encoded to BC on a worker. In a page encoding takes seconds, so textures went up uncompressed (RGBA8 with every mip level, 22 MB for a 2048 side). The dashboard's car has two 4096 images; this was most of the startup memory and a good part of the load time, on both targets.\n\n**What now**\n- `bcpack` (tools/bcpack/run.sh model.gltf --max 2048) writes `name.color.dds`, `.data.dds`, `.occlusion.dds` or `.normal.dds` beside each image for each way the materials read it: BC1 (BC3 with alpha), BC4 or BC5, every mip level, DDS with a DX10 header (`BcImage` reads and writes it).\n- `Gltf.load` finds the file by its name and makes a deferred `Bitmap` from it (`Bitmap.deferred`): the image is not decoded unless something asks for its pixels, and `MeshTextures` uploads the file as it is, in a page too, where the GPU samples BC. A GPU that cannot, and an image drawn flat, decode it as before. A file larger than `maxTextureSize` is not used; `{compressed: false}` or ASHUI_BC_FILES=0 ignores them.\n- Bitmaps are keyed by a stable `id`, so asking about a texture never decodes the image.\n\n**Measured on the dashboard (same build, the switch only)**\n- Page: ready after 2.1 s against 2.9-3.0 s; the program's shared memory 606 MB against 716 MB; live heap after load 45 MB against 77-79 MB; after eight laps of the pages 207 MB live against 288 MB.\n- Desktop, Vehicle page at 12 s: footprint 530-580 MB against 741 MB; Haxe heap 53 MB against 125-133 MB; 35 frames in the first second against 23.\n- The car looks the same: RMSE 0.0046 against the runtime-compressed 4096 render.\n\n**Left**\n- The page's shared memory is still about 600 MB: it grows to hold what the program allocates before its first collection and never shrinks. ASH_GC_HEAP_MB=400 on the page's address (?env=) brings it to 483 MB; ASH_GC_TRIGGER_MB does nothing there. Where the startup allocation comes from beyond textures is not looked at.\n- BC7 for colour, better than BC1 for gradients, and a quality pass over BcEncoder's endpoints; KTX2 with Basis for a smaller download (the two files are 5.3 MB).\n- bcpack reads .gltf with external images; images inside a .glb or as data URIs have nowhere to put a file.","files":null}]}